  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let,&nbsp;<math><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br />The relation <math><mi>R</mi></math> is defined on set <math><mi>A</mi></math> is<br /><br /><math><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Therefore, <math><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now, <math><mn>6</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>∈</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>A</mi></math> but <math><mo>(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>∉</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>.<br /><br />Therefore, <math><mi>R</mi></math> is not reflexive.<br /><br />It can be observed that <math><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>∈</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> but <math><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>∉</mo><mi>R</mi></math>. Therefore, R is not symmetric.</p><p>Now, <math><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>∈</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> but <math><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>∉</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>. Therefore, <math><mi>R</mi></math> is not transitive.<br /><br />Hence, <math><mi>R</mi></math> is neither reflexive nor symmetric nor transitive</p>",
